# Routing — TanStack Router

## File-Based Routes

TanStack Router uses file-based routing. The file path maps directly to the URL.

```
src/routes/
├── __root.tsx          → / (root layout wrapping all routes)
├── index.tsx           → /
├── about.tsx           → /about
├── auth/
│   ├── login.tsx       → /auth/login
│   └── register.tsx    → /auth/register
└── dashboard/
    ├── index.tsx        → /dashboard
    └── settings.tsx     → /dashboard/settings
```

---

## Root Route

```typescript
// src/routes/__root.tsx
import { createRootRoute, Outlet } from "@tanstack/react-router";

import { RootLayout } from "@/layouts/root-layout";

export const Route = createRootRoute({
  component: RootLayout,
});
```

---

## Page Route

```typescript
// src/routes/dashboard/index.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from "@tanstack/react-router";

export const Route = createFileRoute("/dashboard/")({
  component: DashboardPage,
});

function DashboardPage() {
  return <div>Dashboard</div>;
}
```

---

## Route with Loader (data fetching)

Prefer loaders for initial data — they run before the component renders:

```typescript
// src/routes/products/index.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from "@tanstack/react-router";

import { getProductsService } from "@/services/product.service";

export const Route = createFileRoute("/products/")({
  loader: () => getProductsService(),
  component: ProductsPage,
});

function ProductsPage() {
  // Navigation
  const products = Route.useLoaderData();

  return (
    <ul>
      {products.map((product) => (
        <li key={product.id}>{product.name}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

---

## Dynamic Routes

```typescript
// src/routes/products/$id.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from "@tanstack/react-router";

export const Route = createFileRoute("/products/$id")({
  loader: ({ params }) => getProductByIdService(params.id),
  component: ProductDetailPage,
});

function ProductDetailPage() {
  // Navigation
  const { id } = Route.useParams();
  const product = Route.useLoaderData();

  return <div>{product.name}</div>;
}
```

